# Healthcare Application Requirements for SPOTS

## Pediatric Healthcare Context
SPOTS is designed for children and teens with cancer and their parents. All development must consider:
- Age-appropriate user interfaces
- Parent/guardian consent and oversight
- Healthcare team communication needs
- Emotional sensitivity in design and messaging

## User Roles and Access
- **Children/Teens**: Primary users tracking their feelings and symptoms
- **Parents/Guardians**: Oversight and communication with healthcare team
- **Healthcare Team**: Access to patient data for treatment decisions
- **Administrators**: System management and user support

## Data Privacy and Security
- Follow HIPAA compliance requirements
- Implement proper data encryption
- Ensure secure authentication and authorization
- Maintain audit trails for data access
- Consider COPPA compliance for users under 13

## User Experience Guidelines
- Use age-appropriate language and imagery
- Implement intuitive navigation for different age groups
- Provide clear feedback and progress indicators
- Include help and support features
- Design for accessibility and inclusivity

## Data Tracking Requirements
- Symptom and feeling tracking over time
- Treatment schedule and medication adherence
- Communication logs with healthcare team
- Progress visualization and reporting
- Export capabilities for healthcare providers

## Communication Features
- Secure messaging between families and healthcare team
- Appointment scheduling and reminders
- Treatment plan updates and notifications
- Emergency contact protocols

## Technical Considerations
- Ensure data backup and recovery procedures
- Implement proper error handling for medical data
- Consider offline functionality for critical features
- Plan for scalability as patient base grows
- Regular security audits and updates
